<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Conte et al. (2012), Martin et al. (2009) & He et al. (2014) Drosophila ventral furrow invagination biomechanics — Morphological realism / specimen match: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Unchanged from v2 for the confocal layer: the CC BY 4.0 4-stage transverse micrograph is vendored, SHA-256-verified and automatically segmented (DV/ML 1.0496 -> 0.9217, Delta h = 42 px, MyoII 1.63x, trajectory r = 0.9993) and shown with bounding boxes in Panel F. New Panel G renders the reduced 3D shell with the ventral furrow strip tapering toward both poles, qualitatively matching the dorsal/lateral views of a gastrulating embryo, and Panel I shows the He et al. (2014)-style basal cytoplasmic flow. Deductions: no side-by-side with a longitudinal (sagittal/ventral) micrograph for the new AP profile, so the 0.59 EL extent is compared to a literature number rather than a specimen (-5); the Stokes panel is compared to no image of nuclear positions (-4)." ;
